1
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
She loves everything about her son...except who he is.

2
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Prayers for Bobby is a drama, history, tv movie
film directed by Russell Mulcahy.

3
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Bobby Griffith was his mother's favorite son, the perfect all-American boy growing
up under deeply religious influences in Walnut Creek, California.

4
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Bobby was also gay.

5
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Struggling with a conflict no one knew of, much less
understood, Bobby finally came out to his family.

6
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Mary Griffith, played by Sigourney Weaver.

7
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Robert Griffith, played by Henry Czerny.

8
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Bobby Griffith, played by Ryan Kelley.

9
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Ed Griffith, played by Austin Nichols.

10
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Joy Griffith, played by Carly Schroeder.

11
00:48:57,000 --> 00:49:03,000
David, played by Scott Bailey.

12
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
Prayers for Bobby is a televised drama film that premiered
on the Lifetime network on January 24, 2009.

13
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:57,000
The film is based on the book of the same name by Leroy F.

14
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:24,000
Aarons, which is itself based on the true story of the life and legacy of Bobby Griffith, a
young gay man who killed himself in 1983 due to his mother's homophobia.

15
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:51,000
Ryan Kelley stars as Bobby Griffith and Sigourney
Weaver portrays his mother Mary.

16
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
The film was watched by more than 6 million
viewers during its two-day initial run.

17
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:45,000
It received positive reviews from critics and was nominated for two Primetime Emmy Awards: Outstanding Television Movie and Outstanding Lead
Actress in a Limited Series or Movie for Weaver, who was also nominated for a Golden Globe Award, and a Screen Actors Guild Award.

18
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:12,000
The film explores themes of coming out, suicide, based on novel
or book, parent child relationship, homophobia.

19
01:24:33,000 --> 01:24:39,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
